## One thing worth flagging first

The working directory was not the repo root but `data/WebTestBench/web_applications_hinted/WebTestBench_0045` — the *hinted* output directory. Since "hinted" could have meant the work was already done, I checked before editing: the copy had **zero** `data-semtag-*` attributes and was byte-identical to `web_applications/WebTestBench_0045`. So it was a clean copy staged for injection, and I did a fresh one.

## What I annotated

A Lovable/shadcn task manager. Five source files changed; all 60 `src/components/ui/*` primitives untouched.

| Screen | Coverage |
|---|---|
| **Index** (header, filters, task list) | `app.header` region, `app.summary`, `tasks.add`, `filters.panel`, Active/Completed toggles + counts, sort select, `tasks.list` collection, `tasks.empty` |
| **TaskItem** (repeated) | title, priority, description, deadline, blocked warning, prerequisites indicator, complete-toggle, edit, delete |
| **Create/Edit dialog** | `task.form` region, heading, title/description/deadline inputs, clear-deadline, priority select + options, prerequisites collection, cancel, submit |
| **404** | `notfound.page`, message, home link |

**Id namespaces:** `app.*`, `filters.*`, `tasks.*`, `task.form.*`, `notfound.*`.

**Collections — both fold.** `tasks.list` with items keyed by `task.id` (`tasks.list.item.4.edit`), and `task.form.prerequisites` keyed the same way. Distinct prefixes, so a task appearing in both the list and the prereq picker doesn't collide.

## Verification

The validator reports **0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 info** across 37 hinted sites. But it explicitly says it can't see DOM ancestry, runtime ids, or portals — which is exactly where shadcn/Radix breaks things — so I ran the app under Playwright:

- **47 hinted elements on index, 70 with the dialog open, zero duplicate ids** at runtime.
- Portalled content (select menus, dialog) **does** carry the attributes — Radix forwards them.
- The prerequisite checkbox hint lands on a **single** `BUTTON role=checkbox data-state=unchecked`, not duplicated onto Radix's hidden bubble input.
- Both `data-semtag-options` strings render correctly.

**Project checks:** `tsc --noEmit` clean, `vite build` succeeds. `eslint` reports 3 errors / 7 warnings — **all pre-existing**, in untouched files (`ui/command.tsx`, `ui/textarea.tsx`, `tailwind.config.ts`). I confirmed this rather than assuming: linting a pristine copy of the original gives the identical 10 problems.

## Judgment calls

- **One non-attribute change.** `TaskFilters` had its three sort options hardcoded as JSX. I lifted them into a `sortOptions` array and mapped it, so `data-semtag-options` derives from the same source that renders the menu (spec §3, anti-drift). This mirrors the `priorityOptions` array already in `TaskForm`, and produces identical DOM. No component prop-widening was needed — every shadcn primitive already spreads `...props`.
- **`DependencyLines` left unhinted.** It's an SVG overlay of curved connector lines. It's decorative and its hover tooltips duplicate the `.blocked` / `.prerequisites` observables already on each task, which are addressable by id.
- **Existing `data-task-id` left alone** — `DependencyLines` queries on it at runtime, so removing it would break behavior. It's inert to the extractor.

I removed `dist/` afterward but kept `node_modules/` (gitignored, and every sibling app has it).

